messages.content:
{
  "message": "I’m sorry you’re dealing with this while traveling—let’s get your mobile data working at excellent speed if possible. Here’s my plan: (1) I’ll check your line on our side to make sure roaming is enabled and that you haven’t hit any data limits or suspensions. (2) I’ll guide you through a few quick checks on your phone that often fix slow/no data while abroad. To get started, please share: • The phone number of the line that’s having issues • Are you currently in France right now? With your permission, if I find that international roaming is OFF on your line, I’ll enable it at no cost. While I pull up your line, please run these quick checks on your phone and paste the results back here (verbatim is best): 1) Run check_network_status — I’m looking for: • Airplane Mode (ON/OFF) • Signal strength (none/poor/fair/good/excellent) • Network type (e.g., 5G/4G/3G) • Mobile Data (Enabled/Disabled) • Data Roaming (Enabled/Disabled) 2) Run run_speed_test — Tell me the result (unknown/very poor/poor/fair/good/excellent). 3) Run check_vpn_status — Is any VPN connected? 4) Run check_data_restriction_status — Is Data Saver ON? These tell me whether the phone itself is blocking/limiting data (Data, Roaming, Data Saver, or VPN), whether you’re on a fast network type (4G/5G), and what real-world speed you’re getting. Once I have your phone number and those results, I’ll: • Verify and (if needed) enable roaming on your line • Check for data-cap issues and offer a refuel if you’re out of data • Guide you to set 4g_5g_preferred, turn off any limiting settings, and reconfigure APN if needed • Re-test to confirm we reach an Excellent speed."
}

