messages.content:
{
  "message": "I can help get your mobile data working at Excellent speed. Because you’re abroad, the most common causes are (1) data roaming not enabled on either the phone or the line, (2) plan data limits reached or a suspended line, or (3) a phone setting like network mode, Data Saver, VPN, or APN misconfiguration. I’ll check your account/line while you run quick fixes on the phone so we cover both sides.",
  "what_i_need_from_you": {
    "required": [
      "Your mobile phone number (the one you’re using in France)"
    ],
    "optional": [
      "Permission for me to enable international data roaming on your line if I find it’s off (no cost)",
      "If you prefer name lookup instead of phone number: your full name and date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD)"
    ]
  },
  "while_i_verify_your_account_please_do_these_on_the_phone": [
    {
      "step": "Confirm service and basic toggles",
      "why": "Airplane Mode or mobile data OFF will stop data completely; Roaming must be ON when abroad.",
      "how": [
        "Make sure Airplane Mode is OFF.",
        "Make sure Mobile Data is ON.",
        "Turn Data Roaming ON."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "Do you see signal bars and a 4G/LTE/5G icon in the status bar?",
        "Was Data Roaming already ON, or did you have to enable it?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Optimize network mode",
      "why": "For best speeds, the phone should prefer 4G/5G networks.",
      "how": [
        "In Cellular/Mobile Network settings, set Preferred Network Type to 4G/5G (often called 5G On/Auto or 4G/5G Preferred)."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "What option is currently set?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Disable throttling features",
      "why": "Data Saver or a VPN can severely slow or break data, especially when roaming.",
      "how": [
        "Turn OFF Data Saver (sometimes under Network & Internet > Data Saver).",
        "If a VPN is connected, disconnect it."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "Was Data Saver ON?",
        "Was a VPN connected?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Quick reset of radio",
      "why": "Refreshing the cellular registration can restore a good connection.",
      "how": [
        "Toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds, then turn it OFF and wait 30–60 seconds.",
        "After it reconnects, check if 4G/5G returns."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "Did the network type change or improve after this?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Run a speed test",
      "why": "We need to confirm current performance. Anything below Excellent is considered slow.",
      "how": [
        "Use any speed test app/site over mobile data (no Wi‑Fi)."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "The result (or if it says No connection)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "APN check (only if data is still slow or broken)",
      "why": "Incorrect APN/MMSC can break or cripple data while roaming.",
      "how": [
        "In Mobile Network > Access Point Names, choose your carrier’s default APN. If unsure, use Reset to default.",
        "After resetting APN, reboot the phone."
      ],
      "tell_me": [
        "Did you reset APN and reboot? Any change afterward?"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_i_will_check_on_my_side": [
    "Verify your line is active (not suspended) and that international data roaming is enabled on the line. If it’s off, I’ll enable it at no cost (with your permission).",
    "Check whether you’ve hit your plan’s monthly data limit for this line. If you’re out of data, I can add up to 2 GB of data (charged per your plan’s refuel rate) or help you change to a higher‑data plan.",
    "Confirm there are no overdue bills causing restrictions."
  ],
  "next": "Please reply with your mobile number and whether you authorize me to enable roaming on your line if it’s currently off. Also share the results of the quick phone checks above (status bar icons, roaming/data toggles, network mode, Data Saver/VPN status, and the speed test reading). With that, I can finish the account-side fixes and get you to Excellent speed if the network supports it."
}

