messages.content:
{
  "what_this_means": "Right now your phone is camped on a 2G network with Data Saver ON and a VPN connected. 2G is too slow for modern data and can cause a “No Connection” result. Our goal is to (1) get you onto 4G/5G, and (2) remove device-side limits (Data Saver, VPN) so you can reach Excellent speed. Roaming is enabled on your account and you have fresh high‑speed data, so fixes are now on the device side.",
  "do_these_steps_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Turn OFF Data Saver",
      "how": "Use toggle_data_saver_mode to switch it OFF.",
      "why": "Prevents aggressive background/data restrictions that can break speed tests and slow apps."
    },
    {
      "step": "Disconnect the VPN",
      "how": "Use disconnect_vpn.",
      "why": "VPNs can block or slow traffic, especially on weak/roaming links. We’ll add it back later if needed."
    },
    {
      "step": "Force modern network mode",
      "how": [
        "Use set_network_mode_preference to 4g_only.",
        "Wait ~15 seconds.",
        "Then set_network_mode_preference to 4g_5g_preferred."
      ],
      "why": "This forces the device to leave 2G and re-register on 4G/5G, which you need for Excellent speeds."
    },
    {
      "step": "Refresh the radio",
      "how": [
        "Ensure Mobile Data is ON (use toggle_data if needed).",
        "Toggle Airplane Mode ON for ~20 seconds, then OFF (use toggle_airplane_mode)."
      ],
      "why": "A clean re-attach to the roaming network helps the phone pick a better cell."
    },
    {
      "step": "Reboot the phone",
      "how": "Use reboot_device.",
      "why": "Applies all changes and clears any stuck network state."
    },
    {
      "step": "If still stuck on 2G after reboot, reset APN to defaults",
      "how": [
        "Use check_apn_settings. If APN looks incorrect or MMSC is missing, use reset_apn_settings.",
        "After resetting APN, use reboot_device again."
      ],
      "why": "Incorrect APN can block data entirely; a reset restores the correct roaming settings."
    },
    {
      "step": "Last resort if still no improvement: reseat SIM",
      "how": "Use reseat_sim_card, then reboot_device once more.",
      "why": "Ensures the SIM is read correctly and forces a fresh network registration."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "After Step 4 or the reboot, what does the status bar show now? (signal bars and network type: 5G/LTE/4G/3G/2G/E/R)",
    "Run a speed test and share the result category (Excellent/Good/Fair/Poor/Very Poor) and any Mbps shown.",
    "If it still shows 2G after Step 3, tell me immediately so I can adjust the next actions."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Roaming is enabled on your line and you have 1.9 GB of fresh high‑speed data available through 2025-02-28.",
    "Excellent speed requires at least 4G/5G. These steps are specifically to move you off 2G and remove device-side bottlenecks."
  ]
}

