  "explanation": "Yes—toggling Airplane Mode forces a fresh registration with the roaming network and rebuilds data/MMS sessions. Since roaming is enabled, APN/MMSC is set, data is excellent, and VPN/Wi‑Fi Calling/Data Saver/permissions are all OK, this is the next best step. If that doesn’t work, reseating the SIM and testing alternate recipients are the final device-side checks before I escalate.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "action": "Refresh network registration",
      "do": [
        "toggle_airplane_mode ON",
        "Wait ~15 seconds",
        "toggle_airplane_mode OFF"
      ],
      "then": [
        "Run check_network_status and paste the output (confirm 4G/LTE, Mobile Data ON, Data Roaming ON).",
        "With Wi‑Fi still OFF, send a small test MMS and report if it sends or stays on “sending.”"
      ],
      "reason": "Forces a clean reattach and rebuilds the data/MMS context with the roaming partner."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "only_if_still_stuck": true,
      "action": "Reseat the SIM",
      "do": [
        "reseat_sim_card"
      ],
      "then": [
        "Once service returns, run check_network_status again.",
        "Try sending the MMS again and report the result."
      ],
      "reason": "Ensures the SIM profile is read cleanly after the APN reset and reattach."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "only_if_still_stuck": true,
      "action": "Recipient checks",
      "do": [
        "Send an MMS to your own number.",
        "Send an MMS to a different contact."
      ],
      "reason": "Rules out recipient- or thread-specific routing issues while roaming."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "optional": true,
      "action": "Try reverting to 4g_5g_preferred after Step 1 or 2",
      "then": [
        "Run check_network_status and re-test MMS."
      ],
      "reason": "After a clean reattach, some networks behave better on 5G; others on LTE. This helps confirm."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_share_back": [
