{
  "message": "Thanks for checking. Since data was refueled but MMS still fails, let’s run through the key MMS prerequisites on your phone. I’ll guide you step by step and explain why each step matters.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs working mobile data, correct APN/MMSC settings, suitable network mode (not 2G), and no interference from Wi‑Fi Calling, VPN, or Data Saver. We’ll verify each in order and apply fixes where needed.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Confirm mobile data is actually working (not Wi‑Fi)",
      "why": "MMS uses mobile data. If mobile data isn’t active, MMS will hang on “sending.”",
      "do": [
        "Turn OFF Wi‑Fi.",
        "Use check_network_status to confirm Mobile Data is ON.",
        "Open a browser and try loading a website, or use run_speed_test.",
        "If it fails, use toggle_data to turn Mobile Data OFF, wait 10 seconds, then turn it back ON and try again."
      ],
      "tell_me": "Can you load a webpage or does the speed test show any speed? If not, what happens?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Check signal and network type",
      "why": "Very weak signal or 2G can block MMS.",
      "do": [
        "Use check_status_bar to confirm: Airplane Mode is OFF, there is at least some signal, and network shows 4G/LTE/5G (not 2G).",
        "If it shows 2G or unknown, use check_network_mode_preference and set_network_mode_preference to \"4g_5g_preferred\"."
      ],
      "tell_me": "What network type do you see (e.g., 5G/4G/2G) and how many bars?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify APN/MMSC settings",
      "why": "A missing/incorrect MMSC URL is a very common MMS failure point.",
      "do": [
        "Use check_apn_settings and look for the MMSC URL.",
        "If MMSC is missing/blank or flagged incorrect, use reset_apn_settings to restore defaults.",
        "After resetting APN, use reboot_device to restart the phone before testing again."
      ],
      "tell_me": "Is the MMSC URL present? If you reset APN and rebooted, does MMS send afterward?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Temporarily disable Wi‑Fi Calling",
      "why": "In some cases, Wi‑Fi Calling interferes with MMS.",
      "do": [
        "Use check_wifi_calling_status.",
        "If ON, use toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF temporarily and test MMS again (with Wi‑Fi still OFF for this test)."
      ],
      "tell_me": "Was Wi‑Fi Calling ON, and did turning it OFF help?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Check VPN",
      "why": "A VPN can block or slow MMS traffic.",
      "do": [
        "Use check_vpn_status.",
        "If a VPN is connected, use disconnect_vpn, then test MMS again."
      ],
      "tell_me": "Was a VPN active, and did disconnecting it help?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Turn off Data Saver",
      "why": "Data Saver can restrict background data that MMS relies on.",
      "do": [
        "Use check_data_restriction_status.",
        "If Data Saver is ON, use toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF, then test MMS."
      ],
      "tell_me": "Was Data Saver ON, and did turning it OFF help?"
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm messaging app permissions",
      "why": "The messaging app needs storage and SMS permissions to handle MMS.",
      "do": [
        "Use check_app_permissions with app_name=\"messaging\".",
        "If storage or sms permissions aren’t granted, use grant_app_permission for \"storage\" and \"sms\".",
        "Test sending an MMS again."
      ],
      "tell_me": "Were any permissions missing, and did granting them fix it?"
    }
  ],
  "next": "Please start with Step 1 and let me know the results. If Step 1 succeeds (you can browse on mobile data), try sending an MMS. If it still fails, proceed to Step 2, then Step 3, and so on, reporting what you see after each step. I’ll adapt the troubleshooting based on your findings."
}

