messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for trying the APN reset and reboot. Since mobile data and SMS both work, and Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF, the next most common causes are app permissions/restrictions, Data Saver, VPN, or an APN MMSC field that didn’t repopulate. I’ll walk you through quick Android checks in order, with reasons.",
  "steps_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Confirm Messages app permissions",
      "why": "MMS needs access to SMS and storage/photos to attach/send media.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Apps > (Your texting app: Google Messages/Samsung Messages) > Permissions.",
        "Allow: SMS (or Messages), and Photos/Media/Storage.",
        "Go back to the app info screen afterwards."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Enable background/unrestricted data for the Messages app",
      "why": "If background data is blocked, MMS may fail silently.",
      "how": [
        "In the same app info screen: Mobile data & Wi‑Fi (or Data usage).",
        "Turn ON Background data.",
        "Turn ON Unrestricted data usage (if you see that option)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn OFF Data Saver (system-wide)",
      "why": "Data Saver can block MMS or app background transfers.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver.",
        "If ON, turn it OFF.",
        "Alternatively: Settings > Connections > Data Saver (on some Android builds)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Disconnect any VPN",
      "why": "Some VPNs interfere with MMS routing.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > VPN.",
        "If a VPN shows as Connected, disconnect it.",
        "Also check your status bar for a key/lock icon indicating VPN."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Double-check the APN shows an MMSC URL",
      "why": "After a reset, the active APN should have a non-empty MMSC field. If it’s blank, MMS can’t send.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Mobile Network/Cellular > Access Point Names.",
        "Tap the active APN. Look for MMSC (MMS server).",
        "If the MMSC field is empty, let me know—I'll handle next steps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify Preferred network type is 4G/5G",
      "why": "Ensures the device uses a suitable network for MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Mobile Network > Preferred network type.",
        "Choose 4G/5G (5G or LTE/5G Auto)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Test again",
      "why": "Check if changes resolved it.",
      "how": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile Data ON.",
        "Send one small photo MMS to yourself or a contact.",
        "Report what happens (any spinner or immediate failure)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Which texting app are you using (Google Messages, Samsung Messages, or another)?",
    "After Step 1 and 2, were SMS and Photos/Media/Storage permissions allowed and was Background/Unrestricted data enabled?",
    "Was Data Saver ON or OFF? Any VPN connected?",
    "In the APN, is the MMSC field present or empty?",
    "After these steps, did an MMS send successfully?"
  ],
  "notes": "If the MMSC field is empty after the reset, that’s likely the blocker. Tell me, and I’ll take care of the next step for you."
}

