messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the clear update, John. Since your phone now has excellent 5G service with data and roaming ON but your messaging app reports it cannot send MMS, the most likely cause is the MMS server (MMSC) in the APN settings or an app/feature interfering. We’ll check the APN first, as that’s the most common fix. These steps are safe and won’t affect your photos.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "title": "Check APN/MMSC settings",
      "why": "MMS requires a valid MMSC URL in the APN. If it’s missing/incorrect, MMS won’t send.",
      "what_to_do": [
        "On your phone, run: check_apn_settings",
        "Tell me what it shows for: APN name and whether an MMSC URL is present."
      ],
      "what_to_report_back": [
        "APN name",
        "Is an MMSC URL present? (yes/no)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "If MMSC is missing or looks wrong: reset APN, then reboot",
      "condition": "Do this only if Step 1 shows MMSC missing/incorrect.",
      "why": "Resets APN to our defaults, restoring the correct MMS server settings.",
      "what_to_do": [
        "Run: reset_apn_settings",
        "Then run: reboot_device",
        "After reboot, wait ~60 seconds, keep Wi‑Fi OFF, ensure Mobile Data + Data Roaming are ON.",
        "Try sending one photo message to yourself again."
      ],
      "what_to_report_back": [
        "Whether an MMSC was present before the reset",
        "Result of the MMS send after the reboot"
      ],
      "reassurance": "This is safe and reversible; it doesn’t touch your photos."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "If MMSC was present and MMS still fails: check Wi‑Fi Calling",
      "why": "Wi‑Fi Calling can sometimes interfere with MMS routing, especially when roaming.",
      "what_to_do": [
        "Run: check_wifi_calling_status",
        "If it shows ON: run: toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF",
        "Retry sending the photo message"
      ],
      "what_to_report_back": [
        "Wi‑Fi Calling status",
        "Whether MMS sent after turning it OFF"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "If still failing: verify messaging app permissions",
      "why": "The app needs Storage and SMS permissions to send MMS.",
      "what_to_do": [
        "Run: check_app_permissions for your messaging app (usually named “Messages” or “Messaging”)",
        "If storage or sms aren’t granted, run: grant_app_permission for storage and sms",
        "Retry sending the photo"
      ],
      "what_to_report_back": [
        "Which permissions were missing (if any)",
        "Result after granting and retrying"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "title": "Carrier-side roaming refresh (optional next)",
      "why": "Re-provisions roaming on our side; can help if everything else looks correct.",
      "what_I_can_do": [
        "You previously approved this. If you want, I can refresh roaming on your line now.",
        "After I do it, please toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds and then OFF, then retry sending the photo."
      ],
      "what_to_report_back": [
        "Whether you want me to perform the roaming refresh now"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Please run Step 1 now (check_apn_settings) and tell me the APN name and whether an MMSC URL is present.",
    "If you’d like me to refresh roaming on your line right away while you check APN, say the word and I’ll do it."
  ],
  "thought_process": "Your connectivity is excellent, so the failure is almost certainly configuration-specific to MMS. The APN’s MMSC is the top culprit; resetting APN and rebooting resolves most cases. If that’s fine, we rule out Wi‑Fi Calling interference and ensure the messaging app has Storage and SMS permissions. As a final step, I can refresh roaming on our side and have you rescan networks."
}

